problems.problem:
Determine all integers $a$, $b$ such that
$$(a+b)^n=a^n+b^n$$

(a) for $n=2$;

(b) for $n=3$;

(c) for $n>3$.

Consider a close-packed triangular arrangement of discs of radius $1$ in the plane, in which any two of the discs have at most one point in common. Let $n$ (with $n>1$) be the number of discs on one side of the triangle. The figure shows the case $n=5$.

Compute, in terms of $n$:

(a) the number of points of contact between two discs;

(b) the number of (white) regions enclosed by discs;

(c) the total area of these regions.

